-- Gossip options without a BroadcastText get the client's own one, so the option text is shown in every client locale.
-- 2451 gossip_menu_option rows have OptionBroadcastTextID = 0, so the core sends OptionText (English) to every client
-- (GossipDef.cpp: the BroadcastText value is used when the id is set, gossip_menu_option_locale otherwise, and that table is
-- nearly empty). For 1381 of them the English OptionText is byte-identical to the English Text of exactly one
-- BroadcastText row of build 70338 that has a translation. This sets that id. Only rows that still have id 0 and the same
-- text are touched; options with several candidate ids, a match only on the female variant (Text1) or no translation are
-- left as they are. Safe to run again (a second run changes 0 rows).
